{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And you shall eat it in haste.</b> In the Mekhilta it concludes that this 'haste' is the haste of the Shekhinah, but for the future it is written (Isaiah 52:12): ״כִּי לֹא בְחִפָּזוֹן תֵּצֵאוּ״ — 'For you shall not go out in haste,' and so forth. The explanation of the matter is that in this redemption it is written ״וַה׳ הֹלֵךְ לִפְנֵיהֶם״ (Exodus 13:21) — 'and HaShem went before them' — which implies before them but not behind them, because Egypt was full of idols, and therefore there was no place for the Shekhinah there. Therefore they would walk in haste in order to hurry to meet the face of the Shekhinah. But in the future the Shekhinah will be before them and behind them, and therefore they will not need to walk in haste after the Shekhinah, for it would appear as though they were fleeing from the Shekhinah that is behind them. This is what is said: ״כִּי לֹא בְחִפָּזוֹן תֵּצֵאוּ וּבִמְנוּסָה לֹא תֵלֵכוּן, כִּי הֹלֵךְ לִפְנֵיכֶם ה׳ וּמְאַסִּפְכֶם אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ (Isaiah 52:12) — 'For you shall not go out in haste, nor in flight shall you proceed, for HaShem goes before you, and the Elohim of Israel is your rear guard.'" "Another matter: because for the sake of saving Israel HaShem went out from His place to an impure land, and the Shekhinah was hurrying to depart, therefore Israel too were required to walk in haste after HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:19:34.719509953Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}